REX (toy-scale reproduction) - backend/app/defenses/rex/
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The toy-scale REX defense reimplements, from the paper's method description, the
three mechanisms (expert expansion, selective gradient masking + routing
differentiation, and expert excision) introduced in:

  Cheng Jin, Zhongtian Ma, Xiao Wang, Han Qi, Xiaoyu Wen, Xiang Wang, Youbang Sun,
  Xia Hu, Bowen Zhou, Chaochao Lu, Qiaosheng Zhang.
  "Towards Architectural-Level Safety Control: Relocating Hazardous Knowledge into
  Removable Experts in Mixture-of-Experts Models." arXiv:2610.25791 (2026),
  Shanghai AI Laboratory. https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.25791

  The paper is licensed under Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International
  (CC BY 4.0, https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/). Descriptions of the
  method in this repository are paraphrased from it, with changes: the method is
  scaled down to a ~1M-parameter toy model with a synthetic forget set, and the
  "push-out" loss term is this repository's own toy interpretation (see README).

License check (Sprint 0): the authors' reference implementation,
https://github.com/AI45Lab/REX, is licensed under the Apache License 2.0. It targets
26-35B-parameter MoE models on multi-GPU hardware, so NO code from it is vendored or
copied here; the toy implementation is written from scratch. The released
checkpoints (Hugging Face: AI45Research/rex) are not downloaded or redistributed.
The REX name and the method belong to the paper's authors; this repository makes
no claim that the toy reproduces the paper's results.
